NOTICE
======

Authorship and AI assistance
----------------------------
This is personal reverse-engineering of the author's own Pocophone F1, done for
interoperability (getting the fingerprint sensor working under mainline Linux /
postmarketOS).

A large part of the work in this repository — the reverse-engineering analysis,
the kernel driver, the probe scripts, and the notes — was produced with the help
of an AI coding assistant (Anthropic Claude). It has been reviewed by the author,
but readers and downstream projects should be aware of it. Some upstream projects
forbid or restrict AI-assisted contributions; check the target project's
AI-contribution policy before submitting any of this material to it. (For example,
postmarketOS does not accept AI-generated contributions.)

Excluded proprietary material
-----------------------------
This repository deliberately does NOT contain, and must not be used to redistribute:

  * The signed Qualcomm/Goodix TrustZone applications and libraries
    (gfber, fpcber, cmnlib / cmnlib64 — the .mdt and .b0* segment files).
  * The vendor Android HIDL fingerprint service binary.
  * Qualcomm, Sony, or Xiaomi/MiCode reference source used during analysis.

Those are the property of their respective owners. Extract the TrustZone blobs
your build needs from your own device's firmware. The .gitignore in this repo is
configured to keep them out of version control.

Redacted material
-----------------
Device-specific key material and tokens captured during analysis (e.g. the raw
keymaster fingerprint key bytes and sensor device tokens) have been redacted from
the notes. Only the protocol structure — field offsets, lengths, status codes — is
documented.

Warranty
--------
Provided as-is, with no warranty. Probing TrustZone and the serial engine on this
SoC can hang the device; see the safety section of the README.
